flexglue-doppelganger demo — NOTICE

This directory (apps/flexglue-doppelganger/) is a thin CPU clear-experiment
around the public ONNX export of FlexGlue
(https://github.com/cvg/FlexGlue, MIT — see LICENSE-UPSTREAM).

Demo scripts, the experiment harness, and this documentation are MIT
(see LICENSE). They are not a copy of the FlexGlue training code. The ONNX
call sequence follows upstream onnx/match_pair.py (MIT): SIFT keypoints,
a 512×512 descriptor, then the sparse matcher, which returns matches and a
pair covisibility score.

Upstream (attribution):
  Repo:    https://github.com/cvg/FlexGlue
  Paper:   Lindenberger, Sarlin, Miksik, Pollefeys,
           "FlexGlue: Sparse-to-Dense Feature Matching and Visual Disambiguation",
           arXiv:2610.32976 (2026).
  Weights: GitHub release v0.1 (open download, no Hugging Face login)
           flexglue_descriptor.onnx
           flexglue_matcher.onnx
           https://github.com/cvg/FlexGlue/releases/tag/v0.1
  Not used: flexglue.pth and facebook/dinov3-convnext-base-pretrain-lvd1689m.
           The Hugging Face DINOv3 backbone is gated. This demo does not
           request access and does not route around that gate.

The descriptor ONNX file contains the DINOv3 ConvNeXt-B backbone
(extractor weights). Upstream states that those weights are under the
DINOv3 License, which restricts redistribution and use. The license text
distributed with the FlexGlue release is copied here as DINOv3_LICENSE.md.
Matcher weights other than that backbone are MIT, per the upstream README.
Weights are downloaded at run time into work/ and are not committed.

Evaluation images are a small sample of the Doppelgangers test set
(Cai et al., ICCV 2023; dataset page doppelgangers.cs.cornell.edu;
code repo RuojinCai/doppelgangers, MIT). Images are Wikimedia Commons
files. This demo keeps only CC0 / public-domain / CC BY (no NC, no ND,
no SA) so match visualisations are not forced into share-alike, and it
records each file's Commons URL, author, and license in
experiments/exp1_cpu_covisibility/provenance.md. Images are downloaded
at run time and are not committed.

The upstream demo pair assets/berlin1.jpg + assets/berlin2.jpg (FlexGlue
repo, MIT tree) is an optional qualitative anchor and is not part of the
AUROC.

